Bug Report #5
Title
Like Button for Reply Comments Is Unresponsive
Description
In the comments section under videos, users can reply to other users' comments. Each reply comment includes a Like button that allows users to express appreciation. However, when users attempt to tap the Like button specifically for reply comments, nothing happens. The button does not register the tap — no animation, colour change, or count update — and no network activity is triggered.
This issue does not affect top-level comments, which respond as expected when liked.
Severity
•	Medium
Priority
P2
Component
Comments Section
Environment
•	Browser: Chrome 
•	OS: Windows 11
•	Screen Size :1920x1080
•	Device: Desktop
Steps to Reproduce
1.	Navigate to any video with existing comments and replies 
2.	Locate a reply under a parent comment 
3.	Click the "Like" button on the reply 
Expected Behaviour
The like count should increment and the button should highlight or toggle state
Actual Behaviour
Nothing happens when the "Like" button on a reply comment is clicked
Screenshots/Videos
 Additional Context
This issue appears only for reply-level comments; liking parent comments works correctly.
Suggested Fix
Check if the reply comment object is correctly wired to the like API.
