Bug Report #10
Title
No Warning Message When ‘Comment’ and’ Reply ‘Exceeds 500 Characters
Description
The comment input field and reply field allows users to enter more than 500 characters, but no warning or feedback message is displayed when the limit is exceeded. This may confuse users when their full comment is not saved or displayed correctly. If the input is more than 500 characters, it displays only the first 500 characters.
Severity
•	Low
Priority
P3
Component
Comments section and reply section
Environment
•	Browser: Chrome 
•	OS: Windows 11
•	Screen Size :1920x1080
•	Device: Desktop
Steps to Reproduce
1.	Navigate to the comment input field.
2.	Enter text longer than 500 characters.
3.	Observe that no warning or character limit feedback is shown.
Expected Behaviour
A warning should appear once the character count exceeds 500, such as:
❗ Comment too long. Limit is 500 characters. (Current: 537)
Actual Behaviour
Users can type beyond 500 characters with no warning, potentially leading to confusion or data truncation.
Screenshots/Videos
 

Suggested Fix
Display a real-time character counter below the input field (e.g., 432 / 500 characters).
Show a red warning message when the count exceeds 500.

